                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Top-right (many journals; Taher Fig 5)." .


###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_stage> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                          rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation> ;
                                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/struct> ;
                                                          rdfs:label "per_stage (CouplingStageEvaluation)" ;
                                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "per_stage" ,
                                                                                                         "recompute_coupling_per_stage" ;
                                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Re-evaluate the coupling at every integrator stage — the coupling is a full part of the vector field (standard ODE integration). Accurate; required to reproduce reference integrators for stiff / chaotic / multistable systems. (tvboptim maps this to recompute_coupling_per_stage=True; diffrax already recomputes the whole RHS per stage.)" ;
                                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "per_stage" ;
                                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "per-stage coupling evaluation"@en ;
                                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Re-evaluate the network coupling term at every stage of a multi-stage integrator. Costlier, but the coupling seen by each stage is consistent with that stage's state; the difference from per-step matters for stiff or chaotic coupled networks."@en ;
                                                          <https://w3id.org/tvbo/backendParameter> "tvboptim: recompute_coupling_per_stage=True" .


###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation#per_step> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                         rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/tvbo/CouplingStageEvaluation> ;
                                                         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/struct> ;
                                                         rdfs:label "per_step (CouplingStageEvaluation)" ;
                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "per_step" ;
                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Evaluate the coupling once per integration step and hold it constant across the stages — a TVB-style efficiency shortcut (the coupling reduction runs once per step). Faster but lower- order in the coupling; can change the trajectory for sensitive systems. (tvboptim: recompute_coupling_per_stage=False, the current backend default.)" ;
                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "per_step" ;
                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "per-step coupling evaluation"@en ;
                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Evaluate the network coupling once per integration step and hold it frozen across the integrator's stages. The default, and the classic TVB treatment."@en ;
                                                         <https://w3id.org/tvbo/backendParameter> "tvboptim: recompute_coupling_per_stage=False" .


