<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepDirection#down> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                            rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepDirection> ;
                                            rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/struct> ;
                                            rdfs:label "down (SweepDirection)" ;
                                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Decrease the parameter monotonically (high to low), once." ;
                                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "down" .


###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepDirection#up
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepDirection#up> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                          rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepDirection> ;
                                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/struct> ;
                                          rdfs:label "up (SweepDirection)" ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Increase the parameter monotonically (low to high), once." ;
                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "up" .


###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#from_previous> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding> ;
                                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/struct> ;
                                                   rdfs:label "from_previous (SweepSeeding)" ;
                                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Each point is seeded from the final state of the preceding point, so the trajectory follows the solution branch as the swept parameter changes quasi-statically. Forces sequential, order-dependent execution (emitted as a scan, not a vmap). Used to reach a working point by slowly ramping a parameter (e.g. global coupling) and, with sweep_direction, to expose hysteresis / multistability. Sweep-granularity analogue of InitialStateMethod.from_branch." ;
                                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "from_previous" .


###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding#independent> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                 rdfs:subClassOf <https://w3id.org/tvbo/SweepSeeding> ;
                                                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/tvbo/struct> ;
                                                 rdfs:label "independent (SweepSeeding)" ;
                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Each point is initialised independently from the model's initial values (a cold start), so points are order-independent and may be evaluated in parallel (see parallel_mode). Default; today's behaviour." ;
                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "independent" .


