###  https://w3id.org/tvbo/HemodynamicWarmupRequirement
<https://w3id.org/tvbo/HemodynamicWarmupRequirement> rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> ;
                                                     rdfs:comment "Modelling axiom: for any tvbo:HemodynamicObservation, the discarded transient (tvbo:transient_time) MUST be ≥ the observation's HRF kernel duration (tvbo:hrfKernelDuration). Otherwise the causal HRF convolution is under-filled and the BOLD time axis shifts earlier, so the signal spuriously precedes the stimulus rather than lagging it by the hemodynamic delay. Example: the tvboptim BOLD pipeline uses a 20000 ms kernel (5000 samples at dt = 4 ms) via prepend_history + valid-mode convolution, so transient_time ≥ 20000 ms is required."@en ;
                                                     rdfs:label "Hemodynamic warm-up requirement"@en ;
                                                     rdfs:seeAlso <https://w3id.org/tvbo/HemodynamicObservation> ,
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/tvbo/hrfKernelDuration> ,
                                                                  <https://w3id.org/tvbo/transient_time> ;
                                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Hemodynamic warm-up requirement"@en ;
                                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Observed empirically (TVB-O acoustic-stimulation use-case, 2026): a 15000 ms transient (< 20000 ms kernel) made auditory BOLD precede the loudness by ~1 s with a mislabelled 1043 ms TR; transient ≥ 20000 ms restored a causal hemodynamic lag (≈ +1.5 s) and the correct 1000 ms TR."@en .


